k in a ponytail throughout, and she does not interact with a comb or brush. This part of the answer choice **‘1’ is incorrect**.\n\n---\n\n### ❌ **5. Does she apply makeup?**\n\n- **No.** Although she is looking at a tablet (possibly for makeup tutorial), there is **no visible application of makeup** — no brushes, no powders, no mascara, no lipstick. She does not touch her face with cosmetic tools or products. So, **makeup is not performed** in this sequence.\n\n---\n\n### ❌ **6. Does she do laundry?**\n\n- **Yes — but this is outside the scope of answer ‘1’.** In frames 1–5, she is seen starting the washing machine. The caption even says, “HAD TO WASH MY BABY TOO 😊” — indicating laundry is being done. However, **answer ‘1’ specifically excludes laundry**, which is correct — because the question asks about *what she does in the washroom when she gets up*, and while laundry happens in the same room, it’s a separate activity from the personal hygiene routine. **But since laundry is not part of answer ‘1’, its presence doesn’t invalidate the answer — unless the answer included it, which it doesn’t.**\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Final Evaluation:\n\nAnswer **‘1’** claims: *Wash her face, brush her teeth, and comb her hair.*\n\n- ✅ Wash face — **Confirmed**\n- ✅ Brush teeth — **Confirmed**\n- ❌ Comb/brush hair — **NOT confirmed** — **this is a critical omission**\n\n---\n\n## 🚫 Conclusion:\n\n**The answer ‘1’ is NOT correct**, because it **incorrectly includes “comb her hair”** — an action **not observed** in the frames. While two out of three actions are correct, the inclusion of an unverified third action makes the answer inaccurate per the question’s criteria.\n\n> ✅ **Correct answer should only include actions that are visually confirmed.** Since “comb her hair” is not shown, answer ‘1’ fails the verification.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Suggested Correct Answer (if available):\n\nIf there were an option like:  \n**“Wash her face and brush her teeth”** — that would be accurate.\n\nBut since the question forces us to evaluate **only answer ‘1’**, and it includes an unverified activity, we must conclude:\n\n> **Answer ‘1’ is incorrect.**'}, {'batch_start': 30, 'batch_end': 60, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0154.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0155.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0156.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0157.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0158.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0159.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0160.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0161.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0162.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0163.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0164.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0165.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0166.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0167.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0168.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0169.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0170.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0171.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0172.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0173.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0174.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0175.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs3Y/frames/frame_0176.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/gbDR39yIs